{
  "content_reason": "content_digest leaves out only Lake's .hash files, which cache artifact hashes and which Lake rewrites when it rehashes an unchanged artifact (seen on two files during local builds). Every source, .olean, .ilean, .c and .trace file stays in it. The fetch check uses content_digest; local copies of the pinned backend are still checked against the exact digest.",
  "excluded": "Paths under .lake/config/, .git metadata and the Aeneas release archive",
  "fetch_left_out": [
    ".hash",
    ".trace",
    ".setup.json",
    ".rsp"
  ],
  "fetch_reason": "fetch_digest leaves out Lake build records: files ending in .hash, .trace, .setup.json or .rsp. They hold cached hashes, absolute build paths and command lines, so a backend fetched or built at another path cannot reproduce them, and they are not inputs to any proof or binary. Every source, .olean, .ilean, .c, .so and binary stays in the digest. A fetch at a new path matched every source and artifact and differed only in these records. The fetch check uses fetch_digest; a differing file kind outside this list fails, and the per-kind digests name the kinds that differ. The exact and content digests stay recorded.",
